"""Build the portable five-slide introduction using the retained Web Deck v5 framework."""
from pathlib import Path
import base64
import json
import html
root=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
public=root/'public'
scenarios=json.loads((root/'src/data/scenarios.json').read_text())
def img(i):
 s=scenarios[i-1];p=public/'images/scenarios'/s['game']['image']['filename']
 return f'<img class="story-photo" src="data:image/webp;base64,{base64.b64encode(p.read_bytes()).decode()}" alt="{html.escape(s["game"]["image"]["altText"])}">'
font=''
for w,n in [('Regular',400),('Bold',700)]:
 b=base64.b64encode((root/f'src/fonts/AtkinsonHyperlegible-{w}.woff').read_bytes()).decode()
 font+=f'@font-face{{font-family:LabSans;src:url(data:font/woff;base64,{b}) format("woff");font-weight:{n};font-display:swap}}'
slides=[
('cover current',6,'Trust Under<br>Pressure','The Scholarship Decision Lab',
'<p class="deck-main">Thirty challenges. Two teams.<br>One mission. Protect trust.</p><p class="deck-tagline">Spot the Risk. Plan the Response.<br>Protect the Opportunity.</p>',
'I want us to begin with a person, not a system. This is Sarah, a fictional scholarship applicant. Her application is almost complete, the deadline is close, and the portal has stopped working. Our decisions could protect her opportunity or make the problem worse. Every person and situation in this lab is fictional. The questions are practical ones that scholarship teams may need to discuss. We will examine what we know, identify who could be harmed, and decide what to do. We are not competing for points. We are practicing how to make a better decision together before a real applicant depends on it.'),
('red-slide',1,'Red Team spots the risks','Find what could go wrong.',
'<ul class="intro-bullets"><li>Who could be harmed?</li><li>What are we missing?</li><li>What could make things worse?</li></ul><p class="team-reminder">You are looking for vulnerabilities and consequences. You are not the attacker.</p>',
'I am asking the Red Team to look carefully at the people and the weak spots in the process. In this image, a former reviewer discovers that she can still open applicant records. We can ask who might be harmed, what access should have ended, and what evidence would tell us how far the problem reaches. We do not need to pretend to be hackers. We do need to challenge comfortable assumptions. I will invite several risks, because the technical problem may also affect privacy, fairness, communication, or trust. When we share findings, I want us to explain the consequence and the evidence we would seek.'),
('blue-slide',24,'Blue Team plans the response','Figure out what should happen.',
'<ul class="intro-bullets"><li>What should happen first?</li><li>Who has authority to act?</li><li>How do we keep things working?</li></ul><p class="team-reminder">You protect people, coordinate action, and plan recovery. Your plan still needs scrutiny.</p>',
'I am asking the Blue Team to turn the risks into a practical response. We need an immediate action, a decision owner, and a way to keep essential work moving. In this image, staff coordinate after receiving a vendor incident notice. A quick response can help, but speed alone is not our standard. We should explain why an action helps and what could go wrong with it. We can disagree about the first step while still protecting the same people. I will ask the Red Team to test the plan respectfully. If we are working alone, we can take each perspective in turn and question our own assumptions.'),
('flow-slide',7,'Investigate before you decide','The mission unfolds one stage at a time.',
'<ol class="intro-steps"><li><strong>Know</strong><span>Briefing, facts, and unknowns</span></li><li><strong>Choose</strong><span>Red Team risks, then Blue Team response</span></li><li><strong>Continue</strong><span>A twist, a debrief, and a next action</span></li></ol><p class="team-reminder">Request a clue for evidence. Ask for a nudge to help your thinking. Ask whenever you need support.</p>',
'We will see the mission in stages, so I will not show all the information at once. First we read the briefing and separate confirmed facts from unknowns. The Red Team identifies risks, and the Blue Team selects a response and explains its reasoning. Each team can request a hidden clue. A clue provides scenario evidence or a question to investigate. A nudge is different: it helps our thinking without adding a new fact. Then I will reveal a complication. We can keep our plan or reconsider it. Finally we compare our thinking with the debrief, including tradeoffs and questions that remain open.'),
('final-slide',26,'Leave with a better plan','The goal is a better decision.',
'<ul class="intro-bullets"><li>Discuss with voices, hands, chat, or paper.</li><li>Explain your reasoning. Reconsider when needed.</li><li>Choose one action for the next thirty days.</li></ul><div class="next-step no-advance"><span class="ns-label">Begin together</span><a href="../index.html#mission=6&stage=0&mode=facilitator" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open Thirty Minutes Left</a></div>',
'I will use the projected screen to move us through the mission. We can discuss aloud, raise hands, use chat, or write on paper. Nobody needs an account, a device, or a fast reaction. The optional discussion timer does not submit an answer or end a round. We complete a mission by working through it, rather than selecting one preapproved answer. Some situations allow several defensible responses, and the debrief will help us examine their limits. Before we finish, I want each of us to name one concrete action and an owner for the next thirty days. Let us begin with Sarah and the scholarship deadline.')]
css=(public/'assets/deck-framework.css').read_text()
js=(public/'assets/deck-framework.js').read_text()
skin='''
:root{--navy:#082759;--navy-dk:#071f4a;--navy-md:#2166b1;--steel:#2166b1;--gold:#f5aa0a;--gold-lt:#ffce62;--gold-dk:#9c6200;--lgray:#eef4fc;--mgray:#d9e3f0;--hair:#d9e3f0;--slate:#41546e;--text:#172033;--metal:#f5aa0a;--paper:#fff;--font-display:LabSans,Arial,sans-serif;--font-body:LabSans,Arial,sans-serif}
.slide{background:#f7f8fc}.slide.cover{background:#071f4a}.slide-body{padding:70px 65px 65px;position:relative;height:100%;display:block!important}.slide-footer{font-size:16px}.text-column{position:relative;z-index:2;width:57%;padding-right:20px}.story-photo{position:absolute;right:0;top:0;width:41%;height:calc(100% - 50px);object-fit:cover;object-position:65% 50%;border-left:6px solid #2166b1}.cover .story-photo{border-color:#f5aa0a}.slide h1,.slide h2{font-family:LabSans,Arial,sans-serif;font-weight:700;line-height:1.04;letter-spacing:-1.5px}.slide h1{font-size:72px;margin:15px 0 26px}.slide h2{font-size:58px;margin:18px 0 20px}.intro-subtitle{font-size:30px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.25;color:#082759}.cover .intro-subtitle{color:#ffce62}.cover .deck-main{color:#fff}.deck-main{font-size:32px;line-height:1.3;margin-top:28px}.deck-tagline{font-size:24px;line-height:1.4;color:#e2ebf7;margin-top:28px}.intro-bullets{font-size:32px;line-height:1.3;margin:30px 0 24px;padding-left:30px}.intro-bullets li+li{margin-top:18px}.team-reminder{font-size:24px;line-height:1.35;border-left:4px solid #f5aa0a;padding-left:18px;margin-top:26px}.red-slide .story-photo{border-color:#922b36}.red-slide h2{color:#922b36}.blue-slide .story-photo{border-color:#0a3476}.intro-steps{list-style:none;padding:0;margin:30px 0;display:grid;gap:18px}.intro-steps li{display:grid;grid-template-columns:120px 1fr;gap:10px;font-size:26px;line-height:1.3;padding-bottom:12px;border-bottom:1px solid #d9e3f0}.intro-steps strong{color:#082759}.flow-slide .team-reminder{font-size:23px}.final-slide h2{font-size:58px}.final-slide .intro-bullets{font-size:29px}.next-step{margin-top:28px}.next-step a{font-size:24px}.ns-label{font-size:18px!important}.deck.reflow .slide-body{padding:30px 24px}.deck.reflow .text-column{width:100%;padding:0}.deck.reflow .story-photo{position:relative;top:auto;right:auto;width:100%;height:auto;aspect-ratio:16/9;max-height:300px;border-left:0;border-top:5px solid #2166b1;object-position:65% 50%;margin:25px 0 0}.deck.reflow .slide h1{font-size:3rem}.deck.reflow .slide h2{font-size:2.5rem}.deck.reflow .intro-subtitle{font-size:1.5rem}.deck.reflow .intro-bullets{font-size:1.5rem}.deck.reflow .team-reminder,.deck.reflow .deck-tagline{font-size:1.2rem}.deck.reflow .deck-main{font-size:1.6rem}.deck.reflow .intro-steps li{grid-template-columns:1fr;font-size:1.3rem}.deck.reflow .next-step a{font-size:1.3rem}.slide-body>*{animation:none!important}#notesPanel:not(.open){visibility:hidden}#controls{opacity:1;background:#082759;border-radius:6px;padding:4px}#exitDeck{opacity:1}
'''
body=''
for i,(cls,photo,title,subtitle,content,notes) in enumerate(slides):
 h='h1' if i==0 else 'h2'
 body+=f'<section class="slide {cls}"><div class="slide-body"><div class="text-column"><{h}>{title}</{h}><p class="intro-subtitle">{subtitle}</p>{content}</div>{img(photo)}</div><div class="slide-footer"><span class="brand">Trust Under Pressure</span><span class="fac">The Scholarship Decision Lab</span><span class="url">{i+1} / 5</span></div><div class="notes"><p>{notes}</p></div></section>'
(public/'decks/introduction.html').write_text(f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Two Teams, One Mission | Trust Under Pressure</title><meta name="description" content="A five-slide introduction to Red Team, Blue Team, and the Scholarship Decision Lab."><!-- Built with Web Deck v5 — https://mguhlin.github.io/webdecks/ · Developed by Miguel Guhlin - mguhlin.org · MIT --><meta name="generator" content="Web Deck v5 (https://mguhlin.github.io/webdecks/) — developed by Miguel Guhlin - mguhlin.org"><!-- Images generated for this lab with the built-in image tool. All characters fictional. Full prompts in lab/docs/image-prompts.md. Local fonts embedded under SIL Open Font License. --><style>{font}\n{css}\n{skin}</style></head><body><div class="deck">{body}</div><script>{js}</script></body></html>''')
print('Built five self-contained slides with generated photos, local fonts, teleprompter notes, and Web Deck v5 controls.')
